requent episodes of both hyperglycemia and hypoglycemia.","Her prenatal course was otherwise unremarkable, and she has been compliant with her insulin regimen and prenatal care.","Two hours after admission, she delivers a macrosomic male infant weighing 4,500 grams with Apgar scores of 8 and 9 at 1 and 5 minutes, respectively.","The neonate is noted to be jittery and irritable 30 minutes after birth."]},{"sid":2068,"type":"pmh","lines":["Active Problem List:","- Normal spontaneous vaginal delivery (diagnosed 2020-01-15)","- Type 1 Diabetes Mellitus (diagnosed 18 months prior to current pregnancy)","- Hypothyroidism (autoimmune)"]},{"sid":2069,"type":"psh","lines":["- None"]},{"sid":2070,"type":"medications","lines":["Home Medications:","- Insulin glargine 22 units subcutaneous at bedtime","- Insulin lispro sliding scale 1:10 ratio with meals","- Levothyroxine 75 mcg PO daily","- Prenatal vitamin with iron 1 tablet PO daily"]},{"sid":2071,"type":"allergies","lines":["No known drug allergies"]},{"sid":2072,"type":"family_history","lines":["- Type 1 Diabetes Mellitus in father","- Autoimmune hypothyroidism in mother","- Celiac disease in sister"]},{"sid":2073,"type":"social_history","lines":["Smoking: Never smoker.","Alcohol: None during pregnancy; social alcohol use prior to conception.","Occupation: High school mathematics teacher."]},{"sid":2074,"type":"physical_exam","lines":["On examination, the patient is in moderate distress due to contractions.","Her vital signs are stable, and fetal heart tracing is reassuring.","The obstetric examination reveals that she is 6 cm dilated and 90% effaced."]},{"sid":2075,"type":"labs","lines":["Laboratory Values:","- Neonatal blood glucose: 25 mg/dL","- Hemoglobin: 17 g/dL","- Calcium: 9.2 mg/dL","- Magnesium: 2.1 mg/dL","- Complete blood count: Unremarkable"]}],"orders":[]},{"id":6925,"date":"2021-07-15","type":"inpatient","dept":"Obstetrics & Gynecology","attending":"Dr. Emily Rodriguez","cc":"Sudden sensation of something bet